        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">refractory ceramic</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Ceramic refractories are inorganic, non-metallic materials—primarily oxide or non-oxide ceramics—designed to withstand very high temperatures while maintaining mechanical strength, chemical stability, and resistance to thermal shock, typically used for lining furnaces, kilns, and other high-temperature industrial equipment.</skos:definition>
